  "slug": "acid-scale-66f3",
  "summary": "Tools for malignant cell calling, isoform quantification and CNV atlases address scalability and benchmarking needs in cancer transcriptomics.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is reusable, queryable tooling for transcriptomic and genomic data in cancer and single-cell settings. CATFISHR combines RNA-expression similarity, inferred CNV profiles and consensus cell typing to identify malignant cells, and CNVSIM builds an interpretable copy-number reference atlas of 112 CNV-defined cancer subtypes with calibrated projection of held-out samples. IG-28 targets isoform identification and quantification from large bulk and single-cell full-length cDNA datasets, and OTTER deconvolutes murine host reads from tumor xenograft BS-seq and transcriptomic data. scLncR and LncACTdb 4.0 extend lncRNA analysis to single-cell and ceRNA contexts, BILBO provides self-hosted RNA-Seq analysis, and Verix benchmarks complex structural variant calls. The newest elements are CNV-expression integration for malignant cell identification and a CNV-defined reference atlas for subtyping.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
